{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"7bf7d724e718ee9fbb1cefd38b3d250f98176093996d268942e4a6046d0d143f","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_fbe92c433342cfd8afb01c6a6430e6c6ad703ae0ba296121106a2ac03c1f4eef","overall_assessment":"The paper introduces the predictron, a novel architecture that integrates model learning and value prediction through end-to-end training. The work addresses a significant challenge in model-based reinforcement learning by demonstrating that abstract models can be trained to produce accurate value functions without requiring pixel-perfect reconstruction. The experimental results on mazes and pool show consistent improvements over standard deep network baselines, suggesting the approach has potential to influence future research in model-based learning and planning.","paper_id":"BkJsCIcgl","paper_identity_sha256":"5ef12808d2012e682243fe76ec51536ae1df986d91a05657e2b1687851956426","prompt_identity_sha256":"85857267c6cfa8ac01f9e9a2012a4a74fafcfa30c93a3e5728dbb95c3f98c908","raw_response_sha256":"a76816d0a678e7d27fca27c92c9a371675c9b80ab020fdae825598e7d4a0699d","request_identity_sha256":"57c09e93a0be69080accd16b7375eb354ee9f355710dffea9dd4143a4f61eb43","reviewer_identity_sha256":"32b29c26fbf1508e066dfb25b1a9a3fe0654c5869a7da3020e1e8e61940befe3","role":"SIGN","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"8ce76e56ecfbf9b52d2b64be3d91c483e410ffb8fd9a62aa0edffb721b226e54","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-002","SRC-003","SRC-034"],"review_text":"The work addresses a broadly important problem in artificial intelligence: the integration of learning and planning in model-based reinforcement learning. By proposing an architecture that trains an abstract model end-to-end to predict value functions, the paper introduces a paradigm that could influence multiple research areas, including model-based RL, planning, and representation learning. The focus on abstract models that do not need to correspond to the real environment in a human-understandable way is a significant conceptual advance that may inspire further research in these fields.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-BRD"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-005","SRC-019","SRC-020"],"review_text":"The paper demonstrates the applicability of the predictron in two specific domains: procedurally generated random mazes and a simulated pool environment. In both cases, the architecture outperforms conventional deep network architectures, indicating its potential for use in tasks requiring accurate value prediction. The maze domain highlights the ability of the model to learn complex spatial reasoning, while the pool domain showcases its utility in physics-based simulations. These results suggest that the predictron could be valuable in specialized fields where accurate prediction of future states is critical.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-DOM"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-024","SRC-025","SRC-027"],"review_text":"The paper reports that the predictron consistently outperforms feedforward and recurrent neural network baselines in both the maze and pool domains. The improvements are demonstrated across various architectural configurations, including different depths and the presence or absence of skip connections. The use of median RMSE over five seeds provides a robust measure of performance, and the consistent outperformance across multiple settings suggests that the gains are not due to favorable dataset characteristics. These results indicate a substantial improvement over state-of-the-art methods in the specific tasks evaluated.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-SOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-030","SRC-032"],"review_text":"The paper demonstrates the practical utility of the predictron by showing that its predictions can be used to make decisions in the pool domain. Specifically, the model was used to select initial conditions that maximized the number of pocketing events, resulting in significantly more successful outcomes compared to a standard convolutional network. This suggests that the predictron has potential real-world applications in decision-making tasks where accurate prediction of future events is crucial. However, the paper does not extensively discuss broader societal impacts or risks, focusing primarily on the technical performance of the model.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"1fe926168399acafe41aa65fa3be3c1c158aa317646c09ac7e6400f75a008a3c","paper_id":"BkJsCIcgl","paper_ordinal":49,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"a76816d0a678e7d27fca27c92c9a371675c9b80ab020fdae825598e7d4a0699d","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"BkJsCIcgl","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"3ca8f05c8efa16f6c9603dc46f0f07ddde2516df3e1edf82062789722335e7e1","request_identity_sha256":"57c09e93a0be69080accd16b7375eb354ee9f355710dffea9dd4143a4f61eb43","role":"SIGN","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v6","usage":{"completion_tokens":787,"prompt_tokens":18781,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":19568},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"57c09e93a0be69080accd16b7375eb354ee9f355710dffea9dd4143a4f61eb43","role":"SIGN","role_ordinal":2,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}